Adds CustomVectorSource::invalidateRegion(), matching
CustomGeometrySource::invalidateRegion(). A custom vector source could only
invalidate one tile at a time, so a host whose data changed over an area had to
work out every loaded tile that the area touches. CustomVectorTileLoader now
invalidates each loaded tile that the bounds intersect, at its own zoom, the
same way invalidateTile() invalidates one: the tile fetches again, its cached
data is dropped, and the cancel callback runs
(https://github.com/maplibre/maplibre-native-ffi/issues/1491).
Upstream: not proposed

